From: MaSi <noreply@masi.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: add a PCIe suspend OPP

Give pcie0 a suspend-only OPP so pcie-qcom keeps a nonzero DDR/LLCC
sleep-set contract. Same 1000 kBps floor as SM8550.
MaSi already honours opp-suspend for every SoC in pcie-qcom.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -5625,6 +5625,17 @@
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <16000000>;
 					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_nom>;
 					opp-peak-kBps = <1969000 1>;
 				};
+				
+				/*
+				 * Suspend-only. The synthetic opp-hz keeps link-speed
+				 * matching from selecting it.
+				 */
+				opp-suspend-1 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1>;
+					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <1000 1>;
+					opp-suspend;
+				};
 
 			};
